          "kicker": "Leinster boost",
          "heading": "Leinster welcome back Jamison Gibson-Park as Harry Byrne faces further assessment",
          "body": "Leinster have received a significant boost with Ireland scrum-half Jamison Gibson-Park returning to full training, though the club remain without Harry Byrne and Max Deegan. Gibson-Park is available for Saturday's Cardiff clash after recovering from a groin injury suffered during July's Nations Championship. However, Leinster head coach Leo Cullen will be without Byrne and Deegan as they undergo concussion assessments. They join a lengthy casualty list that includes Ireland internationals Caelan Doris, Jordan Larmour and Joey Carbery."
