          "heading": "Louis Rees-Zammit scores two tries for Bristol Bears in Wales boost",
          "body": "Wales wing Louis Rees-Zammit delivered a commanding performance for Bristol Bears, scoring two tries in a 41-26 victory over Premiership champions Northampton Saints. The 25-year-old's deadly attacking form—including a stunning 50/22 and key defensive plays—comes as a major boost for Steve Tandy ahead of November's Nations Championship. Meanwhile, Dragons hooker Elliot Dee put forward his own international case with a two-try, player-of-the-match display against Scarlets, while young Scarlets wing Macs Page caught the eye as a potential uncapped autumn wildcard."
